[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Fried Liver Attack"]
[Variation "Fried Liver: 7...Ke8"]
[ECO "C57"]
[Character "gambit,sharp"]
[Risk "high"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap,hanging-piece"]
[Themes "king-hunt,f7-pressure"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bc4 Nf6 4. Ng5 4... d5 5. exd5 5... Nxd5 6. Nxf7 6... Kxf7 7. Qf3+
7... Ke8?! { Black retreats the king, but the knight on d5 is now defended only by the queen, and the pin has not gone away. }
8. Bxd5 { Takes the knight. If Black recaptures with the queen, White's queen takes on d5, so Black ends up a piece down. [%cal Gc4d5] } 8... Qf6 { The best try: it offers a queen trade to cover. } (8... Qxd5 9. Qxd5) (8... Qd6 9. Bxc6+ 9... Qxc6 10. Qxc6+ 10... bxc6) (8... Qd7 9. Bxc6 9... Qxc6 10. Qxc6+ 10... bxc6) (8... Be6 9. Bxe6 9... Qd6 10. Bb3)
9. Bxc6 { Takes the other knight with check, so Black has to recapture, and White comes out a piece ahead. [%cal Gd5c6] } 9... bxc6 (9... Qxc6 10. Qxc6+ 10... bxc6 11. d3)
10. Qh5+ { Check, and the queen eyes the pawn on e5. } 10... Qf7 11. Qxe5+ { Wins a pawn with check and keeps the extra piece. } 11... Kd7 12. Qd4 *
